{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>And Balaam went, etc.</b> It intends to say that he did not treat him with honor, but rather Balak went first and he walked after him, and therefore it does not say ״Balak and Balaam went.״ And it is possible that since Balak heard Balaam's statement that he cannot do anything, he turned his back to him and went on his way; only Balaam clung to him from behind and walked with him — and this is what the verse says: <b>And Balaam went with Balak.</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:12:51.793650708Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}